                'A biguanide, metformin, is usually the first-line drug treatment in type 2 diabetes mellitus; however it is contraindicated in patients with an eGFR <30 mL/minute/1.73 m² and should be used with caution if eGFR <45 mL/minute/1.73 m² given the increased risk of lactic acidosis.',
